WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.713
Learn sets the order, and getting
it wrong leaves no gate at all.

2
00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:08.182
You create and switch on the policy
for the authentication context first,

3
00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:10.600
and only then select that context in PIM.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:15.118
If no policy targets it, PIM falls back
to asking for multifactor sign-in,

5
00:00:15.118 --> 00:00:19.713
but that fallback doesn't happen when
the policy is off or only reporting.

6
00:00:19.713 --> 00:00:23.905
And if you also scope the policy to
a directory role, it never applies,

7
00:00:23.905 --> 00:00:27.499
because at activation the person
doesn't hold the role yet.

8
00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:31.630
So this chapter builds the gate, and
leaves selecting it to Chapter 4.
